package zeron.collections;

/// A finite, ordered sequence of values.
///
/// Iteration visits the elements in sequence order, starting at the sequence's initial end, on
/// every call. An `Iterable` promises repeatable traversal but neither order nor finiteness; a
/// `List` promises both, and `Sized` anchors finiteness in the signature. Indexing is not part of
/// the contract, since a linked or fold-based list cannot offer constant-time access.
public contract List<T: mut> requires Iterable<T> + Sized<T> { }
